# Unregistered803 batch/page source candidate

Two fixed internal entry functions enter the existing authenticated outermost snapshot before application lookup, authorize every requested key plus case/policy/config/origin, select exact owner_policy FK records and build one registered worklist internally. No supplied callbacks, worklists, facts or older receipts. They are not registered adapters, routes, agent tools or production effects. Generic impact headers/capture/review locks are untouched.

Page order is normalized full key tuple, then PK. A single global limit+1 sentinel (maximum51 admitted rows) spans keys. Batch detects101 and holds, admitting at most100 total, never100 per key. Sentinels receive the same scope/owner evaluation before trimming. Cursor binds fresh actor, canonical case, config, full key set, purpose/version and last emitted key/PK under dedicated salt/age bound. No token or rows escape a failed operation. Empty pages still authorize every key and repeat the exact empty selector/context before materialization; they create no fake worklist/owner success.

The selector witness has one COMPLETE PIPELINE lifetime: issued for exact selected window, bound once to exact worklist, usable only for necessary same-worklist closure/mapping rechecks, terminal complete/failed. It binds observer/pk/keys/marker/default/raw connection/case/config/purpose/window. Full entry keys remain unchanged; subset selection is allowed only with the exact registered witness. Without it prior discovery and historical-mapping key equality remains unchanged. All global domain/cell/scalar ledgers still charge full entry keys. Copied/old/replayed/failed witnesses cannot start another producer or authorize arbitrary hidden IDs.

One historical scope-only pipeline handles mixed claims/resolutions/retractions. Original-owner permits apply ONLY to claims/resolutions; retractions stay historical with no currentness boolean. Retraction claim relationship/scoped mapping is rechecked after owner evaluation too. Existing owner native predicates and modern-reference engineering holds remain unchanged. This coordinator is a private materialized read result, not current-template selection, source-body visibility or full dependency coverage.

PURE tests use extracted entry/selector and fake ORM/snapshot/signing plus actual extracted scalar equality bridge/producer and mixed owner coordinator. They cover global budgets/order/cursors, empty/full-key authorization, sentinel denial, subset witness lifecycle, exact selection mutations, single mixed pipeline and retraction exclusions. Fake signing does not prove cryptography, fake transport does not prove SQL/native permission semantics. Existing real-ledger/default predicate suites remain intact. Native fixture/SQL/advisory lock/upgrade/capture/review/agent adoption is UNRUN and remains separately blocked. No held action/constructor, main/public payload or existing backup changes.
